D. the rate at which primary consumers moved into the area
        answer: Final Answer: D.

The rate at which primary consumers moved into the area most likely increased, causing more competition for resources among the rodents. This is because an influx of new organisms competing for the same food sources directly leads to heightened competition among existing populations.
